        'rawContent': "{{Starship Information|\n|name = UCS Wildfire\n|image = UCSWildfire1.jpg\n|caption = UCS Wildfire\n|ship_class = UCS Wildfire Class\n|status = Active Naval Service\n|commander = \n|crew = Crew: 350 <br/> Myt'herra: 260\n|processing_system = C4ISTAR Computerized Command, Control, Communications, Intelligence, Surveillance, Target Acquisition and Reconnaissance\n|squadrons = \n|unique = Automated Adaptive Shielding <br/> Leifstein Composite Armor Plating\n}}\n\n---\r\ntitle: \"UCS_Wildfire\"\r 2850\rlatest_revision_id: 7378\r\nlast_updated: \"2007-10-12 18:58:54\"\r\r\ntemplates: []\r---*Career\r\n**Laid down: July 15, 2324\r\n**Launched: March 8, 2325\r\n**Commissioned: UCS Wildfire on March 18, 2325.\r\n**Status: UCS Kriegsmarine Warship\r\n*General Characteristics\r\n**Length: 565 meters\r\n**Beam: 115 meters\r\n**Draft: 105 meters\r\n*Power: 1 x Cybeck 9gW Fusion Reactor\r\n*Propulsion: 5 x Albany Series 9 Gravity Cavitation Drives\r\n*FTL Drive: 1 x GRLD Hyperspace Engine\r\n*Acceleration: 23 KPH/S\r\n*Maximum Velocity: 0.2xC\r\n*Range: Unlimited\r\n*Complement:\r\n**Crew: 350\r\n**Myt'herra: 260\r\n*Sensors: SPAR-95AR Combat Search System\r\n*Processing System: C4ISTAR Computerized Command, Control, Communications, Intelligence, Surveillance, Target Acquisition and Reconnaissance\r\n*Armament:\r\n**2 x GC-9f Fireline Hellguns\r\n**10 Type-R Heavy Blazers\r\n**52 Type-F Blazers\r\n**8 Variable-Ordinance Tactical Missile Tubes\r\n*Defenses:\r\n**Automated Adaptive Shielding\r\n**Leifstein Composite Armor Plating\r\n\r\n[[Image:UCSWildfire1.jpg]]\r\n\r\nWhen the UCS Kriegsmarine began to rebuild after the Mesarthrim Civil War, they decided on several designs to bolster their fleet. The new short-term naval strategy called for a core of frigates, until larger warships could be amassed, but a few heavy cruisers were purchased immediately. The Avenger class from Rahn Industries was selected as the choice heavy cruiser for the Kriegsmarine. The Wildfire was the first delivered in March of 2324, and all subsequent Mesarthrim Avenger classes were considered part of the Wildfire subclass.\r\n\r\nThe Wildfire, along with three other Wildfire class cruisers, were delivered to the Kriegsmarine in March, but the other twelve ordered were never delivered. The Tempest War began, and Rahn Industries cancelled the contracts. One of the Wildfire class vessels was stripped down by the Mesarthrim to be reverse engineered.\r\n\r\nThe Wildfire is extremely well armed. Its heavy weapons payload consists of ten Type-R Heavy Blazers, the heavy anti-warship weapons of the Mesarthrim, as well as a pair of GC-9f Hellguns, a slightly improved model built under license by Fireline Industries on Tincomalee.\r\n\r\n[[Image:UCSWildfire2.jpg]]\r\n\r\nBacking up the Type-Rs are fifty-two Type-F Blazers, the standard anti-ship/anti-fighter cannons of the Mesarthrim. The firepower from these Type-Fs alone is enough to repel most any enemy. Additional firepower comes from eight missile launchers, giving it defense against fighters and also the capability for launching larger anti-warship payloads.\r\n\r\nMesarthrim defenses are superior to the defaults used by Rahn Industries, as are its power sources. The Wildfire and its sister ships can move faster than their Avenger counterparts.\r\n\r\n[[Image:UCSWildfire3.jpg]]\r\n\r\nThe Wildfire served throughout the Tempest War with distinction, delivering troops, escorting convoys, and attacking Prefecture shipping. It was crippled by the FDS Triumph early in the war in the failed attack on New Albany, but was quickly repaired and returned to battle.\r\n\r\n[[Category:Cruisers]]"
