        'rawContent': "{{Starship Class Information|\n|name = Indomitable Class Light Cruiser\n|image = IndomitableClassLightCruiser1.jpg\n|caption = Indomitable Class Light Cruiser\n|designation = Warship Class\n|builder = \n|operator = \n|number_of_ships = \n|crew = 120\n|length = \n|beam = \n|height = \n|powerplant = \n|propulsion = \n|weapons = 8 Naval Autocannons <br/> 36 Fast-Tracking Neutron Cannons <br/> 8 Variable-Ordinance Tactical Missile Tubes\n|armor = \n|shields = \n}}\n\n---\r\ntitle: \"Indomitable_Class_Light_Cruiser\"\r 2915\rlatest_revision_id: 7368\r\nlast_updated: \"2007-10-12 18:38:50\"\r\r\ntemplates: []\r---*Dimensions:\r\n**Length: 390 meters\r\n**Width: 125 meters\r\n**Height: 80 meters\r\n*Acceleration: .62 KPH/S\r\n*Crew: 120\r\n*Troops: 50 Marines\r\n*Other Craft: 2 Shuttles\r\n*Cargo Capacity: 400 Tons\r\n*Armament:\r\n**8 Naval Autocannons\r\n**36 Fast-Tracking Neutron Cannons\r\n**8 Variable-Ordinance Tactical Missile Tubes\r\n*Defensive Systems:\r\n**4 Gradient Gravity Shield Generators\r\n**12 Gravity Stabilizer Couplings\r\n**10 Magnetic Deflector Screens\r\n**Barrier Plasma Shield\r\n**Boron-Nitride Composite Armor\r\n*Sublight Drive: Rahn/Hlow Gravity Cavitation Drive\r\n*FTL Drive: Rahn Industries Rapid Accelerator\r\n*Kovalski-Fahr Drive: Brimston Mk.VII Prototype\r\n\r\n===Overview===\r\n\r\nThe Avenger Class Cruiser was so successful that many consider its low production numbers and high construction costs a liability to the Prefecture Navy.  Fleets rely too much on the heavy cruisers, and are at a tactical loss when they aren't around.\r\n\r\n[[Image:IndomitableClassLightCruiser1.jpg]]\r\n\r\nThe Indomitable was built to fill the gap of firepower, armor, and numbers.  Rahn Industries worked on the prototype cruiser, and the design shows a lot of promise.\r\n\r\n===Capabilities===\r\n\r\nThe Indomitable is well-armed and armored, but not quite like the warship-crushing Avenger.  Hellguns cannot be included on the vessel--they are too costly for a light cruiser.\r\n\r\nThe main punch comes from Naval Autocannons.  The Indomitable carries a lot more than the average frigate, but not as many as an Avenger (when its Hellguns are factored in) or a flagship.  The anti-fighter Neutron Cannon load of an Indomitable is numerous and very powerful.\r\n\r\n[[Image:IndomitableClassLightCruiser2.jpg]]\r\n\r\nThe Avenger and Indomitable have identical missile armaments, though an Avenger can carry significantly more ammunition.  With eight missile tubes, an Indomitable still has plenty of options for combat engagements.\r\n\r\nIndomitables are well-protected compared to frigates, and fast--though not as fast as frigates.  It can take firepower and give it back without having to withdraw early.  All in all, it is an admirable weapons platform and multi-purpose warship.\r\n\r\n===Deployment===\r\n\r\nThe Indomitable itself was finished on March 2nd, 2324.  The line was released in the 2324-2325 overhaul of the Prefecture Navy.\r\n\r\n[[Image:IndomitableClassLightCruiser3.jpg]]\r\n\r\nIn order to save costs, many Vengeance cruisers were replaced with Indomitables instead of Phalanxes.\r\n\r\n[[Category:Cruisers]]"
